or-ling on gemini is the round's most interesting design point and I am recording it though it
did not decide anything: `saturating_sub` is reached only after a guard proves no underflow, so
"a future edit that loosens the guard would silently produce `free_slots = 0` rather than
panicking in debug, corrupting every subsequent launch decision with no diagnostic signal."
Defensive arithmetic hiding a future bug is the same family as everything else in this file.

DECISION. gemini has four more tests. glm has a module contract seven times the size, and it
wrote the critique that found a vacuous partition test in a rival -- a claim I verified by
